From 8112e39c312b14850a8f0df1e3859aaa36c7c0f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maitlandk <maitland@scootnetworks.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:49:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Enable HDMI0 on Turing RK1

The Turing RK1 brings one HDMI transmitter out on its 260-pin SO-DIMM
edge connector: the TMDS clock and data pairs on pins 63-83, and CEC,
HPD and DDC on pins 94-100, where the Jetson SO-DIMM modules it is
pin-compatible with have their HDMI signals. The Turing Pi 2 routes
them to the HDMI connector of its first node. The board device tree
leaves the display pipeline disabled, so nothing drives that port with
a mainline kernel.

Enable the VOP, HDMI0 and its HDPTX PHY, and connect HDMI0 to video
port 0, as other RK3588 boards using HDMI0 do.

The default HDMI0 pin configuration in rk3588-base.dtsi is the only
one the module leaves free: the hdmim1 CEC, SCL and SDA balls
(GPIO0_D1, GPIO0_D5, GPIO0_D4) carry i2c0 and i2c1, which the RK1
device tree uses for its regulators, and the hdmim1 HPD and hdmim2
SCL/SDA balls (GPIO3_D4, GPIO3_C7, GPIO3_D0) are brought out to the
SO-DIMM as GPIOs. The downstream device tree of the vendor's
Rockchip-BSP-based images for this module also uses HDMI0 with these
pins.

No frl-enable-gpios is given, as no FRL enable line is documented for
the module, so the controller runs in TMDS mode only.

No hdmi-connector node is added. This .dts describes the RK1 on a
carrier that is no more than a backplane, and the connector, where
there is one, is on the carrier; dw-hdmi-qp does hotplug detection
and reads the EDID itself.

Signed-off-by: Maitlandk <maitland@scootnetworks.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-turing-rk1.dts   | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-turing-rk1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-turing-rk1.dts
index 7bcad28..065d692 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-turing-rk1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-turing-rk1.dts
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
  */
 
 /dts-v1/;
+#include <dt-bindings/soc/rockchip,vop2.h>
 #include "rk3588-turing-rk1.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -19,3 +20,32 @@
 		stdout-path = "serial9:115200n8";
 	};
 };
+
+&hdmi0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&hdmi0_in {
+	hdmi0_in_vp0: endpoint {
+		remote-endpoint = <&vp0_out_hdmi0>;
+	};
+};
+
+&hdptxphy0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&vop {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&vop_mmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&vp0 {
+	vp0_out_hdmi0: endpoint@ROCKCHIP_VOP2_EP_HDMI0 {
+		reg = <ROCKCHIP_VOP2_EP_HDMI0>;
+		remote-endpoint = <&hdmi0_in_vp0>;
+	};
+};

